msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:20
msgid "**agent** `Agent` - the agent to associate this MockPool with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:22
msgid "Example - Basic MockPool instantiation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:24
msgid ""
"We can use MockAgent to instantiate a MockPool ready to be used to "
"intercept specified requests. It will not do anything until registered as"
" the agent to use and any mock request are registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:34
msgid "Instance Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:36
msgid "`MockPool.intercept(options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:38
msgid ""
"This method defines the interception rules for matching against requests "
"for a MockPool or MockPool. We can intercept multiple times on a single "
"instance, but each intercept is only used once. For example if you expect"
" to make 2 requests inside a test, you need to call `intercept()` twice. "
"Assuming you use `disableNetConnect()` you will get `MockNotMatchedError`"
" on the second request when you only call `intercept()` once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:40
msgid ""
"When defining interception rules, all the rules must pass for a request "
"to be intercepted. If a request is not intercepted, a real request will "
"be attempted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "Matcher type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "Condition to pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "`string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "Exact match against string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "`RegExp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "Regex must pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "`Function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md
msgid "Function must return true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:50
msgid "**options** `MockPoolInterceptOptions` - Interception options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:52
msgid "Returns: `MockInterceptor` corresponding to the input options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:54
msgid "Parameter: `MockPoolInterceptOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:56
msgid ""
"**path** `string | RegExp | (path: string) => boolean` - a matcher for "
"the HTTP request path. When a `RegExp` or callback is used, it will match"
" against the request path including all query parameters in alphabetical "
"order. When a `string` is provided, the query parameters can be "
"conveniently specified through the `MockPoolInterceptOptions.query` "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:57
msgid ""
"**method** `string | RegExp | (method: string) => boolean` - (optional) -"
" a matcher for the HTTP request method. Defaults to `GET`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:58
msgid ""
"**body** `string | RegExp | (body: string) => boolean` - (optional) - a "
"matcher for the HTTP request body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:59
msgid ""
"**headers** `Record<string, string | RegExp | (body: string) => boolean`>"
" - (optional) - a matcher for the HTTP request headers. To be "
"intercepted, a request must match all defined headers. Extra headers not "
"defined here may (or may not) be included in the request and do not "
"affect the interception in any way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:60
msgid ""
"**query** `Record<string, any> | null` - (optional) - a matcher for the "
"HTTP request query string params. Only applies when a `string` was "
"provided for `MockPoolInterceptOptions.path`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:61
msgid ""
"**ignoreTrailingSlash** `boolean` - (optional) - set to `true` if the "
"matcher should also match by ignoring potential trailing slashes in "
"`MockPoolInterceptOptions.path`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:63
msgid "Return: `MockInterceptor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:65
msgid ""
"We can define the behaviour of an intercepted request with the following "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**reply** `(statusCode: number, replyData: string | Buffer | object | "
"MockInterceptor.MockResponseDataHandler, responseOptions?: "
"MockResponseOptions) => MockScope` - define a reply for a matching "
"request. You can define the replyData as a callback to read incoming "
"request data. Default for `responseOptions` is `{}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:68
msgid ""
"**reply** `(callback: MockInterceptor.MockReplyOptionsCallback) => "
"MockScope` - define a reply for a matching request, allowing dynamic "
"mocking of all reply options rather than just the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:69
msgid ""
"**replyWithError** `(error: Error) => MockScope` - define an error for a "
"matching request to throw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:70
msgid ""
"**defaultReplyHeaders** `(headers: Record<string, string>) => "
"MockInterceptor` - define default headers to be included in subsequent "
"replies. These are in addition to headers on a specific reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:71
msgid ""
"**defaultReplyTrailers** `(trailers: Record<string, string>) => "
"MockInterceptor` - define default trailers to be included in subsequent "
"replies. These are in addition to trailers on a specific reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:72
msgid ""
"**replyContentLength** `() => MockInterceptor` - define automatically "
"calculated `content-length` headers to be included in subsequent replies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:74
msgid ""
"The reply data of an intercepted request may either be a string, buffer, "
"or JavaScript object. Objects are converted to JSON while strings and "
"buffers are sent as-is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:76
msgid ""
"By default, `reply` and `replyWithError` define the behaviour for the "
"first matching request only. Subsequent requests will not be affected "
"(this can be changed using the returned `MockScope`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:78
msgid "Parameter: `MockResponseOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:80
msgid ""
"**headers** `Record<string, string>` - headers to be included on the "
"mocked reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:81
msgid ""
"**trailers** `Record<string, string>` - trailers to be included on the "
"mocked reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:83
msgid "Return: `MockScope`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:85
msgid ""
"A `MockScope` is associated with a single `MockInterceptor`. With this, "
"we can configure the default behaviour of an intercepted reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:87
msgid ""
"**delay** `(waitInMs: number) => MockScope` - delay the associated reply "
"by a set amount in ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:88
msgid ""
"**persist** `() => MockScope` - any matching request will always reply "
"with the defined response indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_MockPool.md:89
msgid ""
"**times** `(repeatTimes: number) => MockScope` - any matching request "
"will reply with the defined response a fixed amount of times. This is "
"overridden by **persist**."
msgstr ""

